<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix: Variational Masked Diffusion Models</h2>

<div id="Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix is structured as follows: in <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A VMD Loss Derivation ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> we derive the variational masked diffusion (VMD) loss stated in <a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.1 Basic Variational Formulation ‣ 3 Variational Masked Diffusion (VMD) ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>; in <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Block VMD Loss Derivation ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> we derive the block diffusion loss stated in <a href="#S3.Ex2" title="In 3.2 Block Diffusion Formulation ‣ 3 Variational Masked Diffusion (VMD) ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>; in <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Implementation Details ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> we discuss implementation details; and in <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> we provide additional experimental results.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>VMD Loss Derivation</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we provide the derivation of the VMD loss stated in <a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.1 Basic Variational Formulation ‣ 3 Variational Masked Diffusion (VMD) ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. For this we use the negative evidence lower bound (NELBO) for masked diffusion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al., 2024</a>, Eq. (10))</cite>, <em id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0})\leq\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{NELBO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>NELBO</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0})\leq\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{NELBO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\triangleq\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\left[\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t})\right]dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\triangleq\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\left[\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t})\right]dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{1}{t}\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\left[-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t})\right]dt,\quad\text{with}\quad\alpha_{t}=1-t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>with</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{1}{t}\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\left[-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t})\right]dt,\quad\text{with}\quad\alpha_{t}=1-t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next we derive the NELBO for <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log\int p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t},z)p(z)dz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log\int p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t},z)p(z)dz</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log\int q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t},z)p(z)}{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}dz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log\int q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t},z)p(z)}{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}dz</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\left[-\log\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{i}|x_{t},z)p(z)}{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\left[-\log\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{i}|x_{t},z)p(z)}{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\left[-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t},z)\right]-\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\left[\log\frac{p(z)}{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\left[-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t},z)\right]-\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\left[\log\frac{p(z)}{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\left[-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t},z)\right]+D_{\text{KL}}\left(q_{\phi}(\cdot|x_{0},x_{t})||p(\cdot)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z|x_{0},x_{t})}\left[-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t},z)\right]+D_{\text{KL}}\left(q_{\phi}(\cdot|x_{0},x_{t})||p(\cdot)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We assume <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t},z)=\prod_{i=1}^{L}p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{i}|x_{t},z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t},z)=\prod_{i=1}^{L}p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{i}|x_{t},z)</annotation></semantics></math>. Plugging <a href="#A1.E9" title="In Appendix A VMD Loss Derivation ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> into <a href="#A1.E8" title="In Appendix A VMD Loss Derivation ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0})\leq\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{NELBO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>NELBO</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0})\leq\mathcal{L}^{\infty}_{\text{NELBO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int_{0}^{1}\frac{1}{t}\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\left[\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}}\left[\sum_{i:x_{t}^{i}=\text{{[MASK]}}}-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{i}|x_{t},z)\right]+D_{\text{KL}}\left(q_{\phi}(\cdot|x_{0},x_{t})||p(\cdot)\right)\right]dt." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[MASK]</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int_{0}^{1}\frac{1}{t}\mathbb{E}_{q_{t|0}(x_{t}|x_{0})}\left[\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}}\left[\sum_{i:x_{t}^{i}=\text{{[MASK]}}}-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{i}|x_{t},z)\right]+D_{\text{KL}}\left(q_{\phi}(\cdot|x_{0},x_{t})||p(\cdot)\right)\right]dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a prior distribution over the latent space, often chosen to be a standard Gaussian, <em id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g</em>.<span id="A1.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, in a variational autoencoder setting. Moreover, <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\phi}(\cdot|x_{0},x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(\cdot|x_{0},x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is an approximate posterior parameterized by trainable parameters <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Block VMD Loss Derivation</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">According to <a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.2 Block Diffusion Formulation ‣ 3 Variational Masked Diffusion (VMD) ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}|x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\int p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{&lt;b},z^{\leq b})p(z^{\leq b})dz^{\leq b}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\int p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{&lt;b},z^{\leq b})p(z^{\leq b})dz^{\leq b},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\int q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{&lt;b},z^{\leq b})p(z^{\leq b})}{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}dz^{\leq b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\int q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{&lt;b},z^{\leq b})p(z^{\leq b})}{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}dz^{\leq b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}\log\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{&lt;b},z^{\leq b})p(z^{\leq b})}{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}dz^{\leq b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}\log\frac{p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{&lt;b},z^{\leq b})p(z^{\leq b})}{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}dz^{\leq b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}\left[-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{&lt;b},z^{\leq b})-\log\frac{p(z^{\leq b})}{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}\left[-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{&lt;b},z^{\leq b})-\log\frac{p(z^{\leq b})}{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}\left[-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{&lt;b},z^{\leq b})\right]+D_{\text{KL}}(q_{\phi}(\cdot|x^{b}_{t},x_{0}^{\leq b})\|p(\cdot))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{q_{\phi}(z^{\leq b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{\leq b})}\left[-\log p_{\theta}(x_{0}^{b}|x_{t}^{b},x_{0}^{&lt;b},z^{\leq b})\right]+D_{\text{KL}}(q_{\phi}(\cdot|x^{b}_{t},x_{0}^{\leq b})\|p(\cdot)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a prior distribution over the latent space, often chosen to be a standard Gaussian. Moreover, <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\phi}(\cdot|x^{b}_{t},x_{0}^{\leq b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}(\cdot|x^{b}_{t},x_{0}^{\leq b})</annotation></semantics></math> is an approximate posterior parameterized by trainable parameters <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. Plugging <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>, into the masked diffusion NELBO given in <a href="#A1.E8" title="In Appendix A VMD Loss Derivation ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> yields the bound stated in <a href="#S3.Ex2" title="In 3.2 Block Diffusion Formulation ‣ 3 Variational Masked Diffusion (VMD) ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Synthetic Data</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the synthetic data experiments with both 2-token and 4-token sequences, we use a common model architecture adopted from BD3-LM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arriola et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. The baseline is a block diffusion model with 8 DiT blocks and a hidden size of 64. For the proposed VMD, the decoder backbone remains identical to the baseline with an additional lightweight module to incorporate latent variables to ensure equal inference complexity, while the encoder uses only 2 DiT blocks with all other hyperparameters unchanged. Each block <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> in the data sequence is associated with a 32-dimensional latent variable <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{b}</annotation></semantics></math>. The latent is injected into the decoder by fusing it with the positional embedding through a learnable scaling, followed by adaptive layernorm module across all DiT blocks.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because the sequence lengths and block sizes are very small, we train with a large batch size of 10,000 for 2,000 steps. We use the Adam optimizer with a fixed learning rate of 1e-3. For the uniform data experiments, we set the KL weight to 4.0 to encourage the latent prior to match a uniform distribution. In all other experiments, when the KL weight is around 1.0, the performance is stable. Parameters are initialized with default PyTorch settings, and no additional regularization is applied beyond the KL term.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">During inference, we adopt the top probability remasking strategy. The number of function evaluations (NFE) depends on the specific experiment and is reported in detail in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Controlled Synthetic Data with 2 Tokens ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> and <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Controlled Synthetic Data with 4 Tokens ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Variational Masked Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. All experiments converge within a few minutes on a single NVIDIA L40S GPU.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Sudoku</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the Sudoku experiment, we follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2025)</a></cite> to ensure a fair comparison by adopting the same dataset, model backbone, and training procedure. Specifically, the baseline uses the HuggingFace <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">AutoModelForCausalLM</span> with GPT-2 configuration (<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{layer}}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{layer}}=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{head}}=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>head</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{head}}=12</annotation></semantics></math>, embedding size 384). Our model backbone follows the DiT architecture employed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arriola et al. (2025)</a></cite>. For both the encoder and decoder, we adopt the tiny model configuration provided in their official GitHub repository. We set the encoder and decoder to have 4 and 6 Transformer layers respectively in order to match the model size of the baseline. We further introduce a 128-dimensional latent variable, which is embedded, scaled, and then injected into each of the DiT blocks in the decoder through a shared adaptive layernorm module following the DiT-Air design of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Data is represented by flattening each Sudoku puzzle into a sequence of 81 tokens. During training, the puzzle and its solution are concatenated into a 164-token sequence (81 puzzle + [SEP] token + 81 solution + [EOS] token), and the model is trained to predict the answer portion conditioned on the puzzle portion. This design implies that the latent variable cannot be obtained by taking a simple mean over the entire sequence dimension. Instead, we compute a learned weighted average over hidden states. First, a gating network produces a score for each position, and positions corresponding to the puzzle are masked out. The remaining scores are normalized with a softmax to produce attention weights, and finally, the latent is obtained as a weighted sum of hidden states according to these weights.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Training is performed with batch size 1,024, learning rate 1e-3, cosine learning rate scheduler, and 300 epochs. The dataset consists of 1.8M Sudoku puzzles for training and 0.1M for evaluation. During inference, only the puzzle tokens are provided, and the model generates the answer tokens with the remasking strategy described in the main text.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Text</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the text experiments, we adopt a block structure and use the BD3-LM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arriola et al., 2025</a>)</cite> architecture as our baseline. The model processes sequences of length 256 with 8 DiT blocks and 8 attention heads. Our VMD decoder backbone is kept identical to this baseline to ensure equal inference cost, while the encoder mirrors the same architecture but uses only 4 DiT blocks, with all other parameters unchanged. Each block <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> in the sequence is assigned a 128-dimensional latent variable <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{b}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is embedded, scaled, and then added to the data embedding in the same manner as in the synthetic and Sudoku experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Training is performed with batch size 512 using the AdamW optimizer and a learning rate of 3e-4. We employ a constant learning rate schedule with 2,500 warm-up steps.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Controlled Synthetic Data with 2 Tokens</h3>

